al (F-inverse) 95% confidence intervals (CIs) for birth prevalence of microcephaly were calculated\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"These two rates were compared with a Pearson’s chi-square test for heterogeneity.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The excess number of microcephaly cases was calculated as the number of SDs above the mean number of cases reported during 2000–2014.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Denominator data for estimation of state-level 2015 microcephaly birth prevalence were obtained by averaging the total number of live births\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"All statistical significance levels were set at p≤0.05.\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"outcome_types\"]}", "type": "text"}]}